<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    The RELATIONAL half of the test-support library: the contract suite for
    IAlvoSqlDialect plus the T-SQL fake that proves that seam sufficient. It is a
    separate project from MMLib.Alvo.Testing for one reason, and it is not tidiness.

    IAlvoSqlDialect lives in MMLib.Alvo.Data.EntityFrameworkCore rather than in
    Abstractions, because statement shape is a relational concern and Abstractions is
    required to stay free of one. So a contract suite for it cannot avoid referencing
    that package. Putting it in MMLib.Alvo.Testing put the EF dependency on the whole
    test-support library — and MMLib.Alvo.Testing's own remarks say it earns a package
    when EXTERNAL PROVIDER AUTHORS need the contract suite. Shipping it with an EF
    dependency would hand EF to every consumer of the adversarial and differential
    suites, including an author whose store is not EF-backed at all: that forecloses
    the one audience the package exists for, and §0's provider model is precisely
    about not making the core's consumers adopt one infrastructure choice.

    It also had a measurable local cost: test/Directory.Build.props references
    MMLib.Alvo.Testing from EVERY test project, so all of them resolved
    Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational transitively — including
    MMLib.Alvo.Abstractions.Tests and MMLib.Alvo.Schema.Tests, which deliberately have
    no EF. After this split they genuinely have none again — asserted by
    EfDependencyBoundaryTests.The_shared_test_support_library_does_not_reach_ef_core rather
    than assumed, because the family-wide arch fact matches EF's types by NAME and
    would never have noticed.

    Per docs/architecture/package-boundary.md this package is EARNED rather than
    assumed: a real dependency boundary appeared, which is the trigger that rule
    describes, not a speculative split.

    NOT packable yet, for the same reason MMLib.Alvo.Testing is not: it ships when an
    out-of-repo driver author needs it. When it does, it ships as a companion to
    MMLib.Alvo.Testing, which is why its types stay in the MMLib.Alvo.Testing.Data
    NAMESPACE — a consumer who adds this package finds the dialect suite beside the
    data suites they already have, and nothing they already wrote moves.

    TFM/Nullable/etc. are inherited from Directory.Build.props — do not re-declare here.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The base half, for the sibling contract suites its remarks cross-reference. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="../MMLib.Alvo.Testing/MMLib.Alvo.Testing.csproj" />
    <!-- Where IAlvoSqlDialect and PreImageMutation live. The whole reason this project exists. -->
    <ProjectReference
      Include="../MMLib.Alvo.Data.EntityFrameworkCore/MMLib.Alvo.Data.EntityFrameworkCore.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    A public abstract xUnit test class inherited by every driver's own test project, so
    this library needs the test framework and assertion library directly — it is not
    covered by test/Directory.Build.props, which only applies to projects under test/.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.v3.extensibility.core" />
    <PackageReference Include="Shouldly" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
